ultima1-engine - credits
========================

Ultima I is by Richard Garriott / Origin Systems. This distribution includes no
original game files or extracted game art/audio. Runtime game data and text
are read from your own copy; the spec and tests contain behavioral examples.
This project is independent and is not endorsed by the original creators.
Third-party components keep their own licenses (THIRD_PARTY.md).

Engine code
  The ultima1-engine contributors, 2026. GPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSE).

Enhanced art (assets/enhanced/*.png, manifest.toml)
  Original work made for this project, including the 32x32 vehicles
  (horse, cart, raft, frigate in two frames, aircar, shuttle, time
  machine). CC-BY-SA 4.0, "ultima1-engine enhanced pack contributors"
  (assets/enhanced/LICENSE). The title lettering uses Cinzel Black by
  Natanael Gama (SIL OFL 1.1).

Enhanced sound effects (assets/enhanced/sounds/)
  Synthesized from scratch by our own script. CC-BY-SA 4.0
  (assets/enhanced/sounds/CREDITS).

Music (crates/u1-assets/src/music.rs)
  Ten original compositions written for this project and kept as compact
  scores, rendered at run time by the engine's own chiptune synthesizer;
  no recordings, samples or third-party music. Compositions CC-BY-SA 4.0,
  "ultima1-engine contributors"; the synthesizer code GPL-3.0-or-later.
    title       "Lord British's Realm"   D minor, 76 bpm, loops
    overworld   "Sosaria Afoot"          G major, 128 bpm, loops
    town        "Market Day"             F major, 108 bpm, loops
    castle      "The King's Hall"        C major, 92 bpm, loops
    dungeon     "Below"                  A phrygian, 66 bpm, loops
    space       "Among the Stars"        E dorian, 100 bpm, loops
    lair        "Mondain's Lair"         B harmonic minor, 144 bpm, loops
    victory     "The Gem Shattered"      sting, once
    ending      "Sosaria Restored"       D major, 80 bpm, 16 bars / 48 s, loops
    death       "Fallen"                 sting, once

Pixel-art smoothing (crates/u1-assets/src/qol.rs, scale2x / pixel_art)
  Our own implementation of the published Scale2x/EPX rule (Andrea
  Mazzoleni / Eric Johnston's algorithm description); no third-party code.
  GPL-3.0-or-later as the rest of the engine.
